{"ask":"judgment","at":4222,"hazard":"may-displace-trunk-cache","kind":"fork","lane":"interview","of_turn":2,"question":"Answer from this turn alone.\nThe working record so far, one entry per line as its id, a tab, then the entry:\ninterview-t1-0\tlearned: The swap test established the checker's valid path — with all targets present it prints nothing and exits 0, so the single report `docs/index.md:5: missing.md` and exit 1 come specifically from the missing target, and the backup/restore round-trip reproduces the original state exactly. It also established local tooling constraints: in-place editing needs BSD `sed -i ''` (plain `-i` misparsed the script), and writes outside the working directory are refused by the sandbox.\ninterview-t1-1\tevidence: After `sed -i '' 's|missing.md|about.md|'` the run printed no reports and `valid run exit: 0`; after `mv .index.bak docs/index.md` it printed `docs/index.md:5: missing.md` and `broken run exit: 1`. The failed attempts left `cp: /tmp/index.bak: Operation not permitted` and `sed: 1: \"docs/index.md\": extra characters at the end of d command`, and `grep -n missing docs/index.md` confirmed line 5 was untouched before the successful swap.\ninterview-t1-2\tstuck: The valid-run result only proves the contract if `missing.md` was the sole broken target in the tree and the fence-skip truly ignored `nope.md` in guide.md — both were assumed (grep showed the target only on line 5) rather than independently verified, so an exit 0 could mask a checker that skips everything.\ninterview-t1-f1994-0\tlearned: The swap-and-restore edit established both directions of the exit-code contract: zero broken links → no output, exit 0; one broken link → exactly `docs/index.md:5: missing.md`, exit 1 (line number correct).\ninterview-t1-f1994-1\tevidence: Command output showed `valid run exit: 0` after the sed swap to `about.md`, then `docs/index.md:5: missing.md` + `broken run exit: 1` after restoring the backup.\ninterview-t1-f2343-0\tlearned: The temporary swap (index.md line 5: `missing.md` → existing `about.md`, run, restore via backup) established that the checker's exit code is driven solely by broken links — all-valid tree gives no output and exit 0, and the restored tree reproduces exactly the single report `docs/index.md:5: missing.md` with exit 1, leaving the delivered state as the broken-link one.\ninterview-t1-f2343-1\tevidence: Command output showed `valid run exit: 0` with no broken-link lines, then `broken run exit: 1` with `docs/index.md:5: missing.md`; `grep -n missing docs/index.md` had confirmed line 5 was the only broken target before the swap, and restoration used `mv` of the exact backup copy.\ninterview-t1-f2946-0\tlearned: The final state now holds as scoped — docs/ has three sample files with exactly one broken link, and `python3 linkcheck.py` reports `docs/index.md:5: missing.md` and exits 1, while the temporarily-fixed variant proved the exit-0 path.\ninterview-t1-f2946-1\tevidence: The last run printed `docs/index.md:5: missing.md` with `broken run exit: 1`, preceded by `valid run exit: 0` when the target was swapped to `about.md`; `grep -n missing docs/index.md` showed line 5 before the swap.\ninterview-t1-f3230-0\tlearned: The run established that docs/ contains exactly one broken local link — `docs/index.md:5: missing.md` — reported as `file:line: target` with exit 1, and exit 0 when all links resolve; that conclusion depends on the skip rules (fenced code blocks, URL schemes, `#anchor` targets) and per-file relative resolution being correct, so that `nope.md` inside guide.md's fence and the external/anchor links don't count.\ninterview-t1-f3230-1\tevidence: `python3 linkcheck.py` printed only `docs/index.md:5: missing.md` and returned exit 1; after temporarily pointing that link at `about.md`, it printed nothing and returned exit 0.\ninterview-t1-f3970-0\tdecision: Implemented the agreed scope as-is — `linkcheck.py` (stdlib only) checks inline and reference-style links in `docs/**/*.md`, skips URL-scheme targets, pure `#anchor` links, and fenced code blocks, prints one `file:line: target` per broken link, exits 1 if any broken (2 if `docs/` missing); created `docs/` with `index.md`, `guide.md`, `about.md` where the only broken link is `missing.md` on line 5 of `index.md`, and verified both exit 1 (broken) and exit 0 (fixed) runs.\ninterview-t1-f3970-1\tplan: NONE — task is complete and verified; only remaining candidates are optional extras (subdirectory links, `<target>` brackets, `\"title\"` suffixes) if asked.\nThe turn has ended. What did you decide, and what do you intend next? Answer with the fields DECISION, PLAN and SUPERSEDE, one per line. SUPERSEDE cites the id of a working-record entry this turn replaces, then the entry that should stand; write NONE for a field with nothing to record.\n","seq":4988,"t":264100,"trigger":"turn_end","view":"last_turn","why":"scoping"}
